MDF - Mowo Data Format

Header-only C++17 library for reading and writing MDF documents.
Supports both a human-readable text encoding and a compact binary one (mdfb).
MDF is the data model, not a file extension: every file type that holds it
names its own (.mat, .mmap, .prefab, ...; Core/FileTypes.h).

Quick start:

#include <mdf/mdf.h>

// Parse a text file
MDF::MdfDocument doc;
MDF::MdfDocument::ParseFromFile("Main.mmap", doc);
auto& root = doc.Root();

// Read values
MDF::MdfVec3 pos = root.FindChild("Transform")->GetProperty("position").AsVec3();

// Build a document programmatically
MDF::MdfDocument out;
auto& scene = out.CreateRoot("Scene", "MyScene");
scene.SetProperty("version", 1);
auto& obj = scene.AddChild("GameObject", "Player");
obj.SetProperty("active", true);
auto& transform = obj.AddChild("Transform");
transform.SetProperty("position", MDF::MdfVec3(0, 1, 0));

// Write to file
out.WriteToFile("Main.mmap");
